1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
This is Kristaps Porzingis.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Seven foot three.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,500
One of the most skilled big men in basketball.

4
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:11,500
In 2025, he was diagnosed with POTS.

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
When he stands up, his heart rate can hit nearly 130 beats per minute.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
POTS means a jump of 30 or more, just from standing.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
If it can slow down a seven-footer in the NBA...

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
...think about everyone else who has it.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
POTS is one of the most reported problems in long COVID.

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Right now, about 17 million American adults have it.

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
79 percent say it limits their daily activities.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Between 2 and 4 million are out of work because of it.

14
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
That's about 170 billion dollars in lost wages. Every year.

15
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Harvard economist David Cutler put the total cost at...

16
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
3.7 trillion dollars.

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
For an illness most people think is over.

18
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Porzingis has NBA doctors.

19
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Most people with long COVID don't.

20
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Follow for more.
